After running through the first part of the script at that last part of the Run DEC section I get the following error (see below). Reading the error I thought it might be a problem with my input files so I went back and ran a script with input files that worked a few months ago and I got this same error again. There are no error messages to this point. Also, I tried to forge ahead over the error and that didn't work. Any thoughts on what is causing this and how to fix it?

Thanks,
Rebecca

-- -- -- --

NOTE: Before running optimx(), here is a test calculation of the data likelihood
using calc_loglike_for_optim() on initial parameter values...
if this crashes, the error messages are more helpful
than those from inside optimx().

Error in rcpp_calc_anclikes_sp_COOweights_faster(Rcpp_leftprobs = tmpca_1,  :
  unused arguments (m = m, m_null_range = include_null_range, jts_matrix = jts_matrix)

-- -- -- -- --

